(Nestack Cloud & System Architecture Overview) Tj
T* (Page 2: Vector Embeddings and ChromaDB Storage) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (2.1 Sentence Transformers & Dense Embeddings) Tj
T* (For dense semantic vector representation, Nestack utilizes the all-MiniLM-L6-v2 sentence transformers model. This 384-dimensional embedding model maps semantic meanings into Euclidean space with rapid inference speeds, making it ideal for local CPU execution without paid APIs.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (2.2 ChromaDB Persistence & Indexing) Tj
T* (ChromaDB operates as the primary vector store. Ingested vectors are indexed using Hierarchical Navigable Small World \(HNSW\) graphs with cosine distance metrics. Persistent collections store chunk content, page numbers, and vector embeddings on local disk under the chroma_db directory.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (2.3 High-Throughput Batch Upsert) Tj
T* (Embeddings are computed in batches of 32 to 64 items to optimize tensor memory usage. ChromaDB upserts metadata dictionaries containing page_number and chunk_id alongside raw text.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
